{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFound while surveying the credential-in-argv class for antiviral-agrarian-amurminnow (2026-11-22 PST). Operator-workstation tooling and contributor guidance still put Gerrit credentials on a process command line, where any local user or process monitor can read them while the process runs:\n- `infra/gerrit/service-user.sh` (the bot-token rotation tool): `ssh ... gerrit create-account/set-account --http-password \"$TOKEN\"` (lines 41-55; the new token is in the local ssh argv), `aws ssm put-parameter --value \"$TOKEN\"` (line 66), and `awk -v tok=\"$TOKEN\"` (line 83).\n- `infra/gerrit/smoke-check.sh`, `reviewbot-e2e.sh`, `feature-branch-e2e.sh`, `feature-branch-e2e-scenarios.sh` and `feature-branch-inventory.sh`: `curl -u \"user:$PW\"`, and `git clone`/`git push` or `curl` with `https://user:$PW@host` URLs.\n- `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:783,787`: the Jira cleanup's `curl -u \"${JIRA_USER}:${JIRA_API_TOKEN}\"`.\n- `AGENTS.md:90` (the recommended Gerrit REST snippet) and `CONTRIBUTING.md:268-270` teach `curl --user \"$user:$password\"` / `curl -u \"$USER:$PASS\"`.\n\nThese run on operator hosts, not the review-bot box, so they were kept out of the box-side fix (antiviral-agrarian-amurminnow), which adds a static guard over `src/rebar`; this ticket extends that guard to the files above. service-user.sh is the tool the operator would use to rotate the review-bot token, so fixing it before that rotation keeps the new token out of argv.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `infra/gerrit/service-user.sh` passes the new token to `aws ssm put-parameter` and to the webhooks template render without it appearing in any argv (for example `--value file://` from a pipe, and `ENVIRON` in awk), and sets the Gerrit HTTP password without it appearing in the local ssh argv (for example server-side generation, or the REST endpoint with the body on stdin).\n- [ ] The Gerrit REST examples in `AGENTS.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` pass the credential through `curl -K` from a pipe (or another channel that is not argv), not `-u`/`--user`.\n- [ ] The static guard test added by antiviral-agrarian-amurminnow covers these files and passes."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795413927453535001,"uuid":"84c4660b-6f7c-44a4-9c47-0db81c84bf98"}